{title: 177 - Jesus, Your Blood and Righteousness}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #177 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 177}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Jesus, [D/A]your [G]blood [D/F#]and [C/G]righteousness [D/A]My [Am]beauty [D]are, [G]my [D/F#]glo [Em]rious [D/F#]dress;
[G]Mid flaming [D]worlds, [G]in these arrayed, [Am/C]With [D/A]joy [Am]shall [C/G]Ilift [Em/B]up [Am/C]my [D/A]head.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Bold [D/A]shall I stand in [Am]that [G]great [Em]day,
[G]Cleansed [D/A]and redeemed, no [Am]debt [G]to [Em]pay;
[G]For by [F#7]your [G]cross [D#/A#]absolved [Am/C]I am
[G]From sin [F#7]and [G]guilt, [D#/A#]from [Am]fear and shame.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Lord, [D/A]I believe your [Am]precious [Em]blood,
[G]Which [D/A]at the mercy [Am]seat [G]of [Em]God
[G]Pleads for [F#7]the [G]captives' [C/G]liberty,
[G]Was also shed [D#/A#]in [Am]love for me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]When [D/A]from the dust of [Am]death [G]I [Em]rise
[G]To [D/A]claim my mansion [Am]in [G]the [Em]skies,
[G]This then [F#7]shall [G]be [D#/A#]my [Am]only plea:
[G]Christ Jesus lived [D#/A#]and [Am]died for me.
{end_of_verse}
